.TH tkufilterbar n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkufilterbar
.PP
Per\-column filter bar: one small labelled entry per column. Each field filters its own column; the consumer ANDs the non\-empty fields together. Complements \fBtkusearchbar\fR (a single free\-text box) for spreadsheet\-style multi\-column filtering. The set of columns is dynamic \-\- call \fBsetColumns\fR to (re)build the row, e.g. whenever a new result set is shown.
.SS API
.CS
set w [::tkutils::tkufilterbar::widget .f ?-command cmd? ?-delay ms? ?-width n?]
::tkutils::tkufilterbar::setColumns $w {col1 col2 ...}  ;# (re)build the row
::tkutils::tkufilterbar::columns    $w
::tkutils::tkufilterbar::getFilters $w                  ;# dict {col -> text}, non-empty only
::tkutils::tkufilterbar::getFilter  $w col
::tkutils::tkufilterbar::setFilter  $w col text         ;# programmatic, does not fire
::tkutils::tkufilterbar::clear      $w                  ;# empties all, fires
::tkutils::tkufilterbar::focusFirst $w
.CE
.PP
\fB\-command\fR is called as \fBcmd filters\fR, where \fBfilters\fR is a dict mapping each non\-empty column to its text, in column order. Typing fires it after \fB\-delay\fR ms of inactivity (default 300) and on \fB<Return>\fR; \fBclear\fR fires immediately. \fB\-width\fR is the per\-entry width (default 10).
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
The bar holds no filtering logic itself \-\- it only reports the typed fields. The consumer decides how to match (substring, prefix, numeric comparison ...) and combines the conditions (typically AND).
.IP \(bu
\fBsetColumns\fR discards any previously typed contents.
.IP \(bu
Pairs naturally with \fBtkusearchbar\fR: use the search bar for a free\-text AND search and the filter bar for per\-column conditions, ANDing both.
.PP
Tcl/Tk 8.6 and 9.x.
